points.explanation:
These are the casual, contracted forms of 'must' that you'll hear constantly:

- {〜なければ} → {〜なきゃ}
- {〜なくては} → {〜なくちゃ}

So {帰[かえ]らなければならない} / {帰[かえ]らなければいけない} becomes {帰[かえ]らなきゃならない} / {帰[かえ]らなきゃいけない}, and very often just {帰[かえ]らなきゃ}. 'I've gotta go home.'

The second half ({いけない} / {ならない}) is often dropped, especially when talking to yourself. {なくちゃ} sounds a little softer and is often heard from women and children, but anyone can use it.

These forms are casual — in a meeting or with customers, use {〜なければなりません} or {〜ないといけません}.
